# AR detection rules

Full contract: `docs/ar-architecture.md`. Why these exist: `docs/ar-postmortem.md`.

**Flutter decides what to show. The tracker decides what is there.**

## Identity is an exact lookup, never a score

```dart
// ❌ BAD — this is the 612-line matcher that sank AR attempt #1 (RC-2)
final score = hashScore * 0.22 + hueScore * 0.24 + shapeScore * 0.34;
if (score > 28) return null;
if (margin < 5 && score > 22) return null;
return best.id;

// ✅ GOOD — the tracker already resolved identity; we just map it
Marcador? resolve(String trackerName) => _byTrackerName[trackerName];
```

No perceptual hashes, hue histograms, "edge energy", weighted similarity,
tuned thresholds, nearest-neighbour fallbacks, or hint-based tie-breaking.
No `package:image` at runtime. Dart never decodes camera frames.

## State lives in the sealed `ArSessionState`

```dart
// ❌ BAD — attempt #1's widget fields; every bad combination was a bug
Equipo? _detectedTeam;
bool _demoMode = false;
Timer? _detectionTimer;

// ✅ GOOD
ArSessionState state; // ArPreparing | ArSearching | ArCandidate
                      // | ArLocked | ArLost | ArFailed
```

- Content renders **only** in `ArLocked`. `ArPreparing → ArLocked` is illegal.
- Lock requires the debounce gate (same `trackerName` N times in a row).
- Never add a detection boolean to a widget.

## Keep the plugin behind the seam

Only files in `lib/ar/trackers/` may import an AR plugin. Verify:

```bash
rg -l "ar_flutter_plugin" lib/ | rg -v "^lib/ar/trackers/"   # must print nothing
```

## Failures are typed, Spanish, and escapable

Map every `ArTrackerFailure` to the copy in `docs/ar-architecture.md` §8, always
offering the manual team path. A failed real session becomes `ArFailed` — it
**never** silently falls back to demo mode. Demo mode requires `isDemo == true`,
the `MODO DEMO` badge, and cycling all markers (never one hardcoded club).

"Marker not recognised" is not an error — stay in `ArSearching`.
